mira-session — third-party notices
==================================

This crate follows the session-journal format ideas of the Pi project
(`@earendil-works/pi`, reference commit `a276dabe5`): an append-only JSONL log with a
versioned header, `id`/`parentId`-linked entries, one entry per line, and an idempotent
migration step on load. The translated design comes from Pi's coding-agent session manager
(`packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts`) and from the atomic-commit storage
spine of Pi's `durable` package.

Byte-level interoperability with Pi session files is not a goal, and the crate is not a
line-by-line port. Field names are Mira's own `snake_case`, and the implementation
deliberately fixes the durability gaps that Pi's JSONL storage has today (no `fsync`, no
cross-process lock, no restrictive permissions, silently skipped malformed middle lines)
instead of inheriting them, as required by
[docs/adr/0007-bounded-pi-parity.md](../../docs/adr/0007-bounded-pi-parity.md).

